+### Traps at the repo root — read before touching any of them
+
+Three files at the root will waste your time if you assume they are current.
+They are left in place rather than deleted because they are the operator's, not
+mine; none of them is needed.
+
+| File | |
+|---|---|
+| `nb` | A repository-maintenance script written earlier in this project and **now superseded**. It cost four rounds of debugging because `git am` returns inconsistently on an already-applied patch and `git checkout main` fails while a tracked file is modified. **Do not use it.** The explicit `git pull --ff-only && git am --3way <patch>` flow above is the supported path. |
+| `0001-assurance-core-and-cra-article-14.patch`, `0001-assurance-core-art14-register-and-api.patch` | **Superseded** by `0002-baseline-patches-001-and-002.patch`, which is the applied result of both plus the patch-002 script. Applying either 0001 will fail or duplicate. The chain starts at 0002. |
+| `patch-002-remove-fabricated-compliance.py` | Already applied inside the 0002 baseline. Historical only — but worth reading once: it is the commit that deleted fabricated SBOM hashes and a hardcoded `"integrity": "hash_chain_verified"` literal, and it is why the "if it is not gated in code it is not on the pricing page" rule exists. |
+
+To clear them once you have read this:
+
+```bash
+git rm nb 0001-assurance-core-and-cra-article-14.patch \
+       0001-assurance-core-art14-register-and-api.patch
+git commit -m "Remove the superseded maintenance script and the two 0001 patches"
+```
+
+The `00NN-*.patch` files from 0002 onward are the reproducible history and should
+stay: `HANDOFF.md` §2 and `0002-baseline` are what let a fresh clone be rebuilt
+from scratch.
